1	//! Testing server for the ty language server.
2	//!
3	//! This module provides mock server infrastructure for testing LSP functionality using a
4	//! temporary directory on the real filesystem.
5	//!
6	//! The design is inspired by the Starlark LSP test server but adapted for ty server architecture.
7	//!
8	//! To get started, use the [`TestServerBuilder`] to configure the server with workspace folders,
9	//! enable or disable specific client capabilities, and add test files. Then, use the [`build`]
10	//! method to create the [`TestServer`]. This will start the server and perform the initialization
11	//! handshake. It might be useful to call [`wait_until_workspaces_are_initialized`] to ensure that
12	//! the server side initialization is complete before sending any requests.
13	//!
14	//! Once the setup is done, you can use the server to [`send_request`] and [`send_notification`] to
15	//! send messages to the server and [`await_response`], [`await_request`], and
16	//! [`await_notification`] to wait for responses, requests, and notifications from the server.
17	//!
18	//! The [`Drop`] implementation of the [`TestServer`] ensures that the server is shut down
19	//! gracefully using the LSP protocol. It also asserts that all messages sent by the server
20	//! have been handled by the test client before the server is dropped.
21	//!
22	//! [`build`]: TestServerBuilder::build
23	//! [`wait_until_workspaces_are_initialized`]: TestServer::wait_until_workspaces_are_initialized
24	//! [`send_request`]: TestServer::send_request
25	//! [`send_notification`]: TestServer::send_notification
26	//! [`await_response`]: TestServer::await_response
27	//! [`await_request`]: TestServer::await_request
28	//! [`await_notification`]: TestServer::await_notification
